{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Data Compression", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when talking about Data Compression.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations.  Understand information about data and its structure in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.   Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Infinitives of Purpose in Sentences With Simple Present and Present Continuous", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "To start with, it is necessary to learn to identify verbs in the infinitive form. When we say a verb is in its infinitive form, it is because it is in its basic form; that is, as you find it in a dictionary. For example: go, study, prevent, save, etc.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Apart from saving disk space, nowadays we're compressing data to make communication faster.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm thinking of an example to illustrate this idea.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Data compression refers to the process of removing redundant information from data to utilize less space where we store this information.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It scans the text itself to find text strings and replaces not only words but also prefixes and suffixes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">We can use the infinitive form of a verb to indicate a certain <strong>purpose</strong> or to answer the questions why or what for. To do so, you need to always use the preposition &ldquo;<strong>to</strong>&rdquo; before the action (verb) that expresses your <strong>purpose</strong>. There normally is another verb preceding the goal or <strong>purpose</strong> within your sentence.</p>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<p>Take a look at the following examples:</p> <p><i>There is a compression method that replaces words with numbers <strong>to reduce</strong> the size of files.</i></p> <p><i>Apart from saving disk space, we compress data <strong>to make</strong> communication faster.</i></p> <p><i>&nbsp;</i></p> <p>Notice that the infinitive of purpose construction doesn&rsquo;t need any comma (,), period (.), or semicolon (;).</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>To make a negative statement using an infinitive of purpose, we normally add <strong>not</strong> before <strong>to</strong>.</p> <p><i>We compress the data </i><strong><i>not to</i></strong><i>&nbsp;</i><i>take up a lot of disk space.</i></p>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Be Going to in Affirmative", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">We use <strong>be going to</strong> to talk about future plans and, in general, about events that we predict will take place in the future.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Nicholas is going to introduce the concept of data compression.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm going to tell you a bit about how the different compression methods normally work.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We're going to describe some coding methods now.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">We use <strong>be going to</strong> to talk about future plans and, in general, about events that we predict will take place in the future.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The future with <strong>be going to</strong> in affirmative sentences follows this structure:</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<strong>Subject + verb To Be + going to + main verb (base form) + complement</strong></p> <p><strong>&nbsp;</strong>Example:</p> <p><i>&nbsp;</i><i>This learning object <strong>is going to provide</strong> you with really relevant information about data compression.</i></p>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The last method we're going to talk about is the one that compresses graphic files.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "algorithm", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a series of steps for programming a computer to solve a problem", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Huffman coding is an algorithm that consists of a tree in which there are characters paired in ascending order starting from the least to the most common until the tree is complete.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "character", "type": "name"}, {"content": "letters, numbers, or symbols", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It is not possible to find characters in equal numbers within a text.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "reduce", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to decrease the amount of something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: By assigning the shortest bid codes to the most common characters the text will be reduced.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Look for information about Loosy and Lossless data compression.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a comparative table between these two concepts.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your table with your partners.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I look for information about Loosy and Lossless data compression.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I make a comparative table between these two concepts.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share the comparative table with partners.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "redundant", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that is repetitive", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Data compression refers to the process of removing redundant information from data to utilize less space where we store this information.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "replace", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to substitute or change something for something else", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In this method, numbers replace matching strings to really reduce the size of most text files simply because a number is shorter than a word or phrase.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "shrink", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to become reduced in size, amount, or value", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "There are formats such as GIF which don't shrink significantly by compressing them because they are already compressed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}], "labs": [{"exerci